@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Keep the last row for each order so corrections later in a CSV win. Read the
+  whole file before uploading, retaining first-appearance order and hashing the
+  winning rows.
+
 - Enforce the warehouse's 4,000,000-byte request limit for wide rows while
   preserving upload order. Reject individual rows that cannot fit a request.
 
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d2b8a25..77b3376 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,13 +2,16 @@
 
 Reads vendor order exports (CSV), normalizes the columns, drops duplicate orders and posts the rows to the warehouse HTTP API at `WAREHOUSE_URL`.
 
-The loader streams CSV rows and posts batches of at most 2,000 rows.
+The loader reads the entire CSV before posting sequential batches of at most 2,000 rows.
 Uploads split further as needed to keep each encoded JSON request at or below
 the warehouse's 4,000,000-byte limit. A single row that exceeds this limit raises
 `ValueError`; earlier requests may already have been uploaded.
 Timestamp normalization uses a per-file cache of at most 4,096 values to speed up
 exports with repeated timestamps without retaining all timestamps in memory.
-Deduplication keeps the first occurrence across the entire file; its set of order keys grows with the number of unique orders.
+Deduplication keeps the last row in the file for each `(vendor, order_id)`, so late
+corrections win regardless of timestamp. Distinct orders retain their first-appearance
+order. The loader retains one normalized row per unique order in memory until
+the file has been read; hashes are computed from the winning rows.
 
 Supported vendors: `vendor_a`, `vendor_b`, `vendor_c`.
 
